<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $1.7 mln Feb 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $1.7 mln Feb 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $1.7 million surplus on Feb 13 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 13</p>
<p>Exports: $219.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $275.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $357.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $299.8 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $1.7 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.264 million</p>
<p>Imports: $1.137 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.624 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.314 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $437 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>(-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
